---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { label: "Desktop app", href: "#desktop" },
  { label: "GitHub releases", href: "#github" },
  { label: "Provider CLIs", href: "#providers" },
  { label: "From source", href: "#source" },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Updating"
  description="Keep the Modesto app, its GitHub release channel, and your provider CLIs in step. They update on different clocks."
  currentPath="/docs/updating"
  eyebrow="Reference"
  {toc}
>
  <section id="desktop">
    <h2>Desktop app</h2>
    <p>
      Installed macOS, Windows, and Linux builds update through Modesto’s
      built-in updater. You download once from{" "}
      <a href="/download">the download page</a> or{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/releases">GitHub Releases</a>;
      later versions arrive in-app.
    </p>
    <p>
      macOS builds are Developer ID signed and notarized. If an update is
      offered, install it before reporting a bug against an older desktop —
      security fixes target the latest published stable (or current alpha)
      line.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>Alpha builds still update.</strong>
      <p>
        When the signed 1.0.0-alpha.1 RC is GitHub Latest, existing GitHub
        desktop installs hop forward through the same updater. The RC is useful
        and evolving, not a finished 1.0 claim.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="github">
    <h2>Release notes</h2>
    <p>
      Every shipped tag is listed on the{" "}
      <a href="/changelog">changelog</a> and on GitHub. Read those notes
      before a large jump — permission defaults, provider drivers, and
      workspace layout can change between lines.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="providers">
    <h2>Provider CLIs</h2>
    <p>
      Updating Modesto does not update Claude, Codex, Cursor, or the other
      CLIs. Those binaries belong to their vendors. When a provider card
      shows that a newer CLI is available, update it the same way you
      installed it (Homebrew, npm, the vendor’s installer, or Modesto’s
      in-app install where that path exists).
    </p>
    <p>
      After a CLI update, confirm Modesto still discovers the binary — version
      managers sometimes leave the previous PATH entry behind.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="source">
    <h2>From source</h2>
    <p>
      <code>git pull</code>, <code>bun install</code>, then the same{" "}
      <code>bun run</code> command you used before. See{" "}
      <a href="/docs/development">Local development</a> if you are running
      beside another Modesto instance.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
